# Trivy vulnerability exceptions. Each entry MUST carry a justification and a
# revisit trigger. Keep this list minimal — it is a hole in the HIGH/CRITICAL gate.

# CVE-2026-14456 — OpenSSL (libssl3) denial of service via unbounded memory.
# Source: the distroless/cc-debian12 base image ships libssl3; Debian had no fixed
# version as of 2026-08-20 (unfixable at build time).
# Not reachable here: teecryptor is rustls-only (reqwest with rustls-tls,
# default-features=false) and the dep tree has no openssl-sys/native-tls, so the
# binary never links or calls libssl3 — it is dead base-image code.
# Revisit: drop this line once deb12 publishes a fixed libssl3 (the real fix is to
# move to an OpenSSL-free base — tracked separately).
CVE-2026-14456

# CVE-2026-84782 — OpenSSL (libssl3) information disclosure.
# Source: the distroless/cc-debian12 base image ships libssl3 3.0.20-1~deb12u2;
# Debian had no fixed version as of 2026-10-01 (unfixable at build time).
# Not reachable here, for the same reason as CVE-2026-14456: teecryptor is
# rustls-only and the dep tree has no openssl-sys/native-tls.
# Revisit: drop this line once deb12 publishes a fixed libssl3, or at once if
# openssl-sys or native-tls ever enters Cargo.lock.
CVE-2026-84782
